model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway.poolMembership {
    metadata {
      constraint "The hourly pool migration inventory job also reports the pool ownership population, read-only, in a transaction of its own after the inventory's own read, so a report statement that fails or is cancelled leaves the inventory's reads, outcome and lines exactly as they were. The population is every pair a pool token can name: each record in an organization's basaltPools that names an app id, each recorded app with the organization that owns it, and each pool app an organization owns (a copy of the pool app's source, under any name) with its owner. Each pair is classified by the ownership check's own exported rule, never a second copy of it. The report writes one line after the inventory's own, pool-ownership-v1, with counts by shape, the two shapes that exist only in a token's claim, with no record and no owner behind them, named as not observable, the number of organizations whose metadata is not JSON, and at most 50 pool ids of pairs that would be refused, never organization metadata. It reads at most 1,001 pairs under a 3 s statement limit and sends of each organization's metadata only its basaltPools, once, on that organization's first pair, and it writes the line with complete false and a reason, row_cap, query_failed or report_failed, whenever it could not cover every pair. It changes neither the ownership check's answers nor the inventory's own lines and outcome, and it writes nothing to the database."
    }
  }
}
